  "id": "complexity-theory",
  "term": "complexity theory",
  "definition": "Complexity theory is a way of understanding a system by focusing on how its parts relate to and influence one another, rather than studying each part separately. It examines how interactions, feedback, and self-organization among people, policies, interventions, and their surroundings can produce new patterns and changes over time.",
